    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "22 Clonlea combines the character of a settled residential setting with a beautifully extended interior designed around family life. A striking kitchen and dining extension, two distinct living areas and a landscaped rear garden give this three bedroom semi-detached home an appealing balance of sociable space and quieter places to retreat. Set on The Avenue in Woodpark, the property also enjoys off-street parking and convenient access to the amenities of Ballinteer and Dundrum.\n\nExtending to approximately 117 sq m, the accommodation has been thoughtfully arranged to make everyday living easy. The enclosed entrance porch opens to a welcoming hallway with useful storage, while the bay-fronted living room offers a comfortable setting around a cast-iron fireplace. To the rear, the full-width extension brings together a bespoke OBH kitchen, island breakfast bar and dining area, with a rooflight and generous glazing drawing daylight into the heart of the home. French doors open to the garden, and an adjoining sitting room provides flexible space for family relaxation, a playroom or a snug.\n\nA separate utility area and guest WC complete the ground floor. Upstairs are two double bedrooms, a single bedroom and an extended family bathroom with both a bath and a separate shower. Fitted storage, attic access and the practical garden layout add to the appeal of a home that works as well for busy weekdays as it does for entertaining.\n\nWoodpark is a mature residential neighbourhood with an excellent range of everyday amenities in the surrounding area. Local shops and SuperValu in Ballinteer cater for daily needs, while Dundrum Town Centre offers an extensive choice of shopping, cafés and restaurants. Families have a selection of established schools nearby, including St. Attracta`s Junior and Senior National Schools, Wesley College and St. Tiernan`s Community School. \n\nOutdoor recreation is another strong attraction, with Marlay Park and Ballawley Park providing green space for walks and family outings, and the Dublin Mountains offering further opportunities to explore. Nearby dlr Leisure Meadowbrook adds a 25-metre swimming pool, gym, exercise classes and all-weather pitches, providing plenty of options for keeping active close to home.\n\nTransport connections are a particular advantage. Nearby services include route 16 from Ballinteer (Kingston), linking the area with the city centre and Dublin Airport; route 74, serving Dundrum Luas, Marlay Park and the city centre; and the S8 orbital service, connecting with Sandyford Luas and Dún Laoghaire in one direction and Tallaght and Citywest in the other. Balally Luas is approximately a 20 25 minute walk away via Wyckham Way, offering Green Line connections to St. Stephen`s Green, the city centre and Sandyford. Convenient access to the M50 further broadens commuting options, while the combination of local buses, Luas and nearby amenities makes it easy to plan everyday journeys around work, school and leisure."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Porch\nAn enclosed porch with a sliding glazed entrance provides a sheltered approach to the hall and a practical buffer from the outdoors.\n\nEntrance Hall\nA welcoming hallway with oak-effect flooring, useful understairs storage and additional fitted storage. Stairs lead to the first floor.\n\nLiving Room - 13'0\" (3.96m) x 16'0\" (4.88m)\nA well-proportioned reception room with a bay window overlooking the front garden. Wide-plank oak flooring and a cast-iron fireplace create a warm, comfortable setting, with space for generous seating.\n\nSitting Room - 9'1\" (2.77m) x 13'9\" (4.19m)\nOpening into the kitchen and dining space, this additional reception area provides a versatile family room, snug or play area, keeping everyday activities connected while retaining a distinct seating zone.\n\nKitchen - 10'6\" (3.2m) x 20'0\" (6.1m)\nA bespoke OBH kitchen with extensive grey cabinetry, pull-out storage, a concealed coffee station and Silestone work surfaces. The central island incorporates breakfast seating, while a timber window bench adds an informal place to sit. A large rooflight brings natural light into the extension, and the layout offers excellent preparation and storage space.\n\nDining Area - 7'10\" (2.39m) x 12'6\" (3.81m)\nA bright dining space adjoining the kitchen, with room for a family table and French doors opening directly to the rear garden. The connection to the patio is ideal for outdoor dining and entertaining.\n\nGuest WC\nAccessed through a sliding timber door and fitted with a WC, a counter-mounted wash hand basin, tiled finishes and a heated towel rail.\n\nUtility Room\nA separate utility room with space and plumbing for laundry appliances, shelving and a wall-mounted clothes airer. A sliding door keeps this practical workspace neatly contained.\n\nLanding\nA carpeted landing with access to the bedrooms and bathroom. A pull-down attic ladder provides access to additional storage in the partly floored attic.\n\nBedroom One - 12'4\" (3.76m) x 14'1\" (4.29m)\nA generous double bedroom overlooking the front of the property, with fitted wardrobes and carpet flooring.\n\nBedroom Two - 12'4\" (3.76m) x 11'10\" (3.61m)\nA second double bedroom overlooking the rear garden, with carpet flooring and hot press storage. The external wall has been internally insulated.\n\nBedroom Three - 7'11\" (2.41m) x 8'8\" (2.64m)\nA single bedroom to the front, with carpet flooring and internal insulation to the external wall. Equally suited to use as a nursery or home office.\n\nFamily Bathroom - 9'9\" (2.97m) x 5'9\" (1.75m)\nFinished with white and blue tiling and fitted with a bath, separate shower enclosure with an electric shower, WC and wash hand basin.\n\nFront Garden\nA private driveway provides off-street parking for two cars. Raised granite planters, established planting and hedging soften the approach, with gated side access leading to the rear garden.\n\nRear Garden\nA landscaped, enclosed garden with an artificial lawn, a paved patio and mature planted borders. Boundary walls and trellis create a sheltered setting for relaxing and entertaining, while a timber shed provides useful outdoor storage. An outside tap and lighting add everyday practicality.\n\nNotice\nThese particulars are issued by Mark Kelly & Associates (MKA) on the understanding that all negotiations are conducted through us. They are provided in good faith for guidance only and do not form part of any offer or contract. MKA has not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, services or equipment, and purchasers must satisfy themselves as to their condition and working order. All descriptions, measurements, dimensions, maps, plans, photographs, condition, permissions, licences, access, prices, rents, outgoings and other information are approximate, for guidance only and may be subject to change without notice. Maps and plans are not to scale. Photographs are provided for presentation and guidance purposes. Where appropriate, AI-assisted enhancement, refinement or virtual furnishing may be used to improve presentation or assist purchasers in visualising layout, scale or potential. Such imagery is not intended to materially alter or misrepresent the structure, layout, condition or features of the property. Neither MKA nor its staff or representatives have authority to make or give any representation or warranty in relation to the property.\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Extended three bedroom semi-detached home of approximately 117 sq m </li><li> Full-width rear extension completed in 2017 </li><li> Bespoke OBH kitchen with Silestone worktops and island breakfast bar </li><li> Separate front living room and additional family sitting room </li><li> Utility room and ground-floor guest WC </li><li> Two double bedrooms and one single bedroom </li><li> Family bathroom with separate bath and shower </li><li> Gas-fired central heating and double-glazed windows </li><li> Landscaped rear garden, side access and driveway parking for two cars </li><li> Mature Woodpark setting convenient to schools, parks, Dundrum and transport</li></ul>"
